==English==
{{Webster 1913}}
===Alternative forms===
* [[frightfull]] {{qualifier|archaic}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm|en}} {{term|frightful||afraid|lang=enm}}, from {{etyl|ang|en}} {{term|forhtful||fainthearted, timorous|lang=ang}}, equivalent to {{suffix|fright|ful|lang=en}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en-us-frightful.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# {{context|obsolete|lang=en}}: Full of fright; affrighted; frightened.
#* {{quote-book|author=[[w:William Browne (poet)|William Browne]]|year=1613|title=Britannia's Pastorals|passage=See how the '''frightful''' herds run from the wood.}}
# Full of that which causes fright; exciting alarm; impressing terror; shocking; as, a frightful chasm, or tempest; a frightful appearance.
# {{non-gloss definition|Used as an intensifier}}
#: ''We wasted a '''frightful''' amount of money on renovations.''

